Seeding with embeddings downloads the fastembed model on first run (~100MB).

## Environment

See `.env.example`. Required to actually talk to a model:

| Var | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `FEATHERLESS_API_KEY` | OpenAI-compatible endpoint key |
| `MODEL_NAME` | Your fine-tuned model ID |

Recommended for production: `JWT_SECRET`, `ADMIN_API_KEY`, `DATABASE_URL`.
Optional channels: `TAVILY_API_KEY` (growth agent), `TWILIO_*` (SMS webhook).

## Deploy (Railway, from render.yaml)

1. Push this repo to GitHub.
2. On Railtracks: **New Project → Blueprint → point at this repo**. The
   blueprint provisions the pgvector database and web service together.
3. In the web service **Variables** tab, set `FEATHERLESS_API_KEY` and
   `ADMIN_API_KEY` (and optional `TAVILY_API_KEY`).
4. After first deploy, run once (Railway Shell or `railway run`):